# `.etc/` is the operator's local material: the vault pass, the gateway JWT secret, OAuth client
# secrets, a Firebase service-account private key. It was ignored as `.etc/.*` — DOT-files only —
# so anything landing there under an ordinary name was fully stageable, and a `git add -A` would
# have committed a live private key. Closed by default now, with the one tracked thing re-admitted.
.etc/*
!.etc/scripts/
# `.lmthing/<project>/spaces/` is the REAL space layout the MCP server resolves, and it holds
# tracked fixtures — so `.lmthing/` is deliberately NOT ignored here. `sdk/org` is a submodule
# and ignores its own runtime `.lmthing/` via its own .gitignore (lines 27, 44).
# lmauto: the live raw event stream of an in-flight attempt. It is APPENDED TO for the whole run, in
# a tree where autonomous agents run git commands — a stash/checkout would swap the inode out from
# under the loop's open fd and silently lose the rest of the stream. Keep it untracked while it is
# live; the engine force-adds it at the run-end boundary, once the stream is closed.
automation/instances/*/rounds/**/output.jsonl

# Status-page build data: generated by build-images.yml's publish-pages job and
# deployed as a Pages artifact. The published site is the only durable copy —
# committing it back to main is what the [skip ci]/GITHUB_TOKEN deploy bug came
# from.
gh-pages/data/builds/*.json

# Generated by the tamagui vite plugin into each app it builds (`<app>/.tamagui/tamagui.config.mjs`).
# A build artefact derived from the shared config, never authored.
.tamagui/
